# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intune policy exports - never commit.
#
# Export-DeviceConfigurations.ps1 writes decoded mobileconfig payloads
# (.payload.xml) which can contain certificate material and embedded
# credentials, plus assignment files naming groups and users. These patterns
# are deliberately path-independent so the protection survives someone moving
# the exports folder.
#
# This is what lets the TOOLING under Intune/Configuration/ be tracked. That
# directory used to be ignored wholesale, which kept the exports out but took
# every script with them -- the entire export/analyse/rename toolkit existed
# only on one machine. The rules below exclude the generated output rather than
# the directory that produces it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Export output trees, wherever they land
exports/
**/exports/

# Decoded custom-profile payloads (mobileconfig plists, OMA-URI XML)
*.payload.xml

# Resolved assignment targets (group names, membership rules, UPNs)
*.assignments.json

# Export root artefacts
consolidated-config-profiles.json
export-manifest.json
setting-definitions.json
assignment-filters.json
role-scope-tags.json

# Generated analysis reports
policy-overlap-report.json
policy-overlap-report.md
policy-overlap-report.txt

# Generated naming worksheets and the rename audit trail. These carry live
# policy names and assignment targets, so they are output, not source.
policy-name-proposal.csv
rename-map-*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries and packaged artefacts.
#
# Not source, and in several cases larger than GitHub will accept at all:
# Install-ClaudeMSIX.intunewin is ~490 MB and each .msix around 250 MB against
# a 100 MB per-file limit. They are vendor installers and build outputs, and
# belong in a release or a package feed rather than in git history, where they
# cannot be removed again without rewriting it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.msix
*.intunewin
*.exe
*.log
